<h1 class="whs3">PC Requirements</h1>
<div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center; margin-left:18px;" align="center">
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs4"></div>
<h2 class="whs5"><span>User</span> <span class="subheading11" lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;"><i style="mso-bidi-font-style:normal;">&#160;</i></font></span><span lang="EN-GB">requirements</span></h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Images/computer_user.gif" width="186px" height="154px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
<ul class="whs7">
<li style="margin-left:20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:0px;"><span lang="EN-GB">Experience with Microsoft Windows XP.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:0px;"><span lang="EN-GB">A completed customer training course.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="whs5"><span lang="EN-GB">Hardware</span><span lang="EN-GB">requirements</span></h2>
<p><img src="Images/PC.png" width="150px" height="114px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">These requirements change frequently - please contact Metris for the latest specification.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">I</span>BM PC/AT compatible computer: desktop or laptop.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">2.4GHz or 3.4GHz Intel Pentium 4 CPU or compatible.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">2GB of RAM.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note">Important notes<br>
KUBE v12 FP1 and higher are able to use more that 2GB of memory when run under Windows XP Professional.<br>
<br>
The virtual address space of processes and applications is limited to 2GB unless the /3GB switch is used in the Boot.ini file. The /3GB switch allocates 3GB of virtual address space to an application that uses IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE in the process header (KUBE already meets this requirement.) This switch allows applications to address 1 GB of additional virtual address space above 2 GB. This benefits applications that run on computers with more than 2GB of physical memory, enabling them to keep more data in virtual memory without needing to swap it to disk.<br>
<br>
The following example shows how to add the /3GB parameter in the <span style="margin-left:18px; font-weight:bold;"><b>Boot.ini</b></span> <span style="margin-left:18px;">file to enable application memory tuning:</span><span style="margin-left:18px; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;"><br>
<br>
[boot loader]<br>
timeout=30<br>
default=multi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)\WINNT<br>
[operating systems]<br>
multi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(2)\WINNT="Windows XP Professional" /3GB</span><span style="margin-left:18px;"><br>
<br>
For more information, please refer one of the following sites:<a href="http://www.microsoft.com/whdc/system/platform/server/PAE/PAEmem.mspx"><br>
http://www.microsoft.com/whdc/system/platform/server/PAE/PAEmem.mspx</a></span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;">Video card - any NVIDIA and ATI video card that supports OpenGL hardware acceleration. Tested video cards:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">NVIDIA:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">Quadro FX500</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">Quadro FX Go 1400</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce FX5200</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce2 GTS</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce2 Pro</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce2 MX400</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce4 MX440</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce4 Ti 4200</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">GeForce4 Ti 4600</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle" value="2">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">ATI:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">Radeon 9600</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">Radeon 7200</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle" style="font-size:8pt;">Radeon X700</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet" value="2">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;">20GB hard disk drive &#160;(full installation requires about 650MB).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;">3.5 inch f<span lang="EN-GB">loppy disk drive (if sensor calibration files are distributed on floppy disks).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">CD-ROM drive (if you install KUBE from CD).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">Slots:</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-GB">PCI &#160;(desktop, for MM X/Y/Z).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-GB">PCMCIA - for CardBus PC card &#160;(laptop, for MM Z).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet" value="6">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;">Ports:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-GB">RS-232 serial port &#160;(for FARO/CimCore serial localisers).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-GB">Parallel port &#160;(for parallel port dongle).</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle"><span lang="EN-GB">3 x USB ports &#160;(for KUBE and K-CMM USB dongles and FARO/CimCore USB localisers).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet" value="7">
<p class="bullet" style="margin-left:18px;"><span lang="EN-GB">Network adaptor with Ethernet port &#160;(</span>for MM D/K-Scan).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="whs5"><span lang="EN-GB">Software requirements</span></h2>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Microsoft Windows XP Professional operating system with Internet Explorer 6 or higher.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="Images/WindowsXP.jpg" width="200px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> For maximum performance, there should be a sufficient amount of <a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1">virtual memory</a> on the PC.</p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP177729071" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB">It is not only related to the physical RAM memory installed but also the virtual Memory settings.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB">How to setup your virtual memory (please contact your PC System Administrator if you are unsure about any of these instructions):</span></p>
<ul type="disc" class="whs10">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;"><span lang="EN-GB">Right click on</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>My Computer</b></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:10pt;"><span lang="EN-GB">Select</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>Properties &gt; Advanced &gt; Performance &gt; Settings &gt; Advanced</b></i></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:10pt;"><span lang="EN-GB">Select</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>Virtual memory &gt; Change</b></i></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:10pt;"><span lang="EN-GB">Select</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>‘System managed size’</b></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB">Minimum size of the swap file is 1GB.</span></p>
</div>
